## Backend events

### OnMessageMentioned

Register a Storm module that implements `OnMessageMentioned`. Dispatch runs from `ModuleBE_MessageDB.postWriteProcessing` after persist, **create only**, and only when `(mention ?? []).length > 0`.

**Contract: one dispatch per create.** The payload includes **all** mentioned ids in `mentionedAccountIds` (order = `message.mention`). Do not assume once-per-id.

Do **not** fire this from a preWrite interceptor — a failed write must not dispatch. Mention does not grant Topic ACL.

```typescript
import {Module} from '@nu-art/ts-common';
import type {OnMessageMentioned, MessageMentionedPayload} from '@nu-art/ts-messaging-backend';

export class MyMentionListener_Class
	extends Module
	implements OnMessageMentioned {

	public async __onMessageMentioned(payload: MessageMentionedPayload) {
		// payload.topic, payload.message, payload.mentionedAccountIds
	}
}
```

Add the listener instance to the Storm module list so `Dispatcher` finds it. No listener = no-op.

